    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Convertible at the holder's option at any time into Common Stock at the lesser of (i) 80% of the per-share price paid in a Qualified Transaction (a priced equity financing of at least $1,000,000 with unaffiliated investors) and (ii) a valuation-cap price equal to $6,480,082 divided by the Issuer's fully diluted shares immediately prior to the Qualified Transaction, subject to price-based anti-dilution adjustment. Principal and accrued interest are convertible. Because both prices are set by reference to a Qualified Transaction, which has not occurred, the conversion price and the number of underlying shares are not currently determinable. The amendment did not change the conversion terms.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">On November 11, 2026, the Issuer and SportsAlert Media, LLC executed an amendment, dated November 12, 2026, of the Promissory Note dated April 10, 2026, as approved by the Issuer's Board of Directors on October 16, 2026, with the reporting person abstaining. The amendment, effective as of October 10, 2026, extended the maturity date from October 10, 2026 to the earlier of April 30, 2027 and the closing of a Qualified Transaction; waived the event of default arising from non-payment at the original maturity date; changed the interest rate to 12% per annum from October 10, 2026, in place of the 10% stated rate and the 15% default rate; and added an extension fee of $2,750 to principal, increasing the principal amount from $27,500 to $30,250. The amendment is reported as the disposition of the original note and the acquisition of the amended note. Both transactions were with the Issuer and approved by its Board of Directors and are exempt under Rules 16b-3(d) and 16b-3(e).</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">No cash was paid and no shares were issued in connection with the amendment. The $2,750 extension fee was added to the principal of the amended note.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Held by SportsAlert Media, LLC, of which the reporting person is the managing member and sole owner.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">The amended note matures on the earlier of April 30, 2027 and the closing of a Qualified Transaction.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

